# ── Aashish AI + portfolio · git-ignore ──────────────────────────────
# PII / data hygiene (Aashish_AI_Agent_Prompt_v2.md §17)
.cv-raw.txt
*.docx
data/raw/
data/extracted/
data/processed/
# Stage B instruction data is generated (~31 MB at 40k examples). The
# generator and its manifest are committed; the JSONL is a build output.
data/instruction/sft.jsonl
training/checkpoints/
training/datasets/
experiments/**/*.safetensors
*.pt
*.pth
*.onnx
*.gguf

# ── Trained tokenizer artifacts ──────────────────────────────────────
# The small dev fixture artifact is committed on purpose: the Python test
# suite and `train_smoke.py` read it, so a fresh clone can verify the
# tokenizer contract without retraining.
#
# The P4 16k artifact is committed for a different reason, and the earlier
# reason recorded here was wrong. It said "real P4+ artifacts (12–16k vocab,
# larger corpora) are build outputs and stay out" — but Stage B initialises
# from a Stage A checkpoint whose vocabulary *is* this tokenizer, and
# `train_stage_b.ipynb` read it from `ai/tokenizer/artifacts/stage-a-16k`.
# Nothing that reaches a Kaggle session carried it: the repository dataset
# ships `git archive` output, and this path was excluded, so the notebook's
# cell 3 printed `tokenizer: False`, carried on, and cell 5 died two cells
# later on a missing `meta.json` — a Stage B fault caused by a missing
# Stage A artifact. Measured 2026-10-03.
#
# So it is a deliverable, not a build output: 1.2 MB, and the exported
# browser model needs the same file. Regenerating it means rebuilding the
# whole corpus, which is exactly what a later session cannot do.
ai/tokenizer/artifacts/*
!ai/tokenizer/artifacts/seed-1k/
!ai/tokenizer/artifacts/stage-a-16k/

# ── The exported browser model (§9.3) ────────────────────────────────
# Build output: `inference/export_browser.py --out ai/model-export/<version>`
# quantizes a checkpoint into shards + manifest + tokenizer. It ships from
# `dist/` (tools/build.mjs copies it when present) but is never committed —
# it is derivable from the checkpoint, and a stale copy in the repo would
# silently disagree with the weights it claims to be.
ai/model-export/

# Scratch export used by the §14 model evaluation: the engine decoder reads an
# exported artifact, and re-creating it is one command
# (`npm run eval:export`). The evaluation OUTPUT (docs/EVAL_*.json) is committed.
tmp-eval-export/

# ── Python (training + inference side) ───────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/

# Secrets / env
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Dependencies / build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/

# ── Dev-only probe artefacts (never shipped to the browser) ──────────
# probes themselves are dev tooling; their OUTPUT is noise
probe-*.txt
shots-*.txt
baseline-run.txt
baseline-fps*
pacing.log
pacing.txt
*-fps.txt
fps-*.txt
*.log
docs/BASELINE-*.json
shots/
dev-fps-last.png
probe.out.txt
probe.err.txt
# a redirected `npm run test:py > py-tests.txt`
*-tests.txt
.tmp-body.json

# ── One-off recovery leftovers from the corrupt freebuff session ─────
film3d_recovered_0.js
film3d_firsthalf_f_001ac2.txt

# Agent/tooling state (holds only a project id, never anything to ship)
.freebuff/
# Host linkage, same category — and no host has been chosen yet
# (docs/DEPLOYMENT.md §6). Keeping it out of git is reversible: the file
# stays on disk, and committing it later is `git add -f .vercel`.
.vercel/

# OS / editor
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/
# Kaggle scratch (P4). The dataset tarball is a `git archive` of HEAD -- a
# build output, not source -- and kaggle-push/ holds the pushed notebook, the
# pulled logs, checkpoints and shard tree. Committing any of it put 2,778 files
# and 167 MB into .git; `git add -A` did it, so the rule is here rather than
# relying on staging by hand each time.
/kaggle-push/
/aashish-ai-portfolio.tgz
/output.txt

# `corpus_cache` names its index CACHE.json, and a run aimed at a relative
# --out leaves a 2-byte `{}` in the repository root. Found there on 2026-10-02,
# untracked, from a run before this session; ignored so the next one cannot be
# committed by `git add -A`, which is how 167 MB of scratch got in before.
/CACHE.json
